Installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the TopSpin project.

## What was implemented:

Successfully integrated Vercel Web Analytics into the Next.js App Router project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Files Modified:

1. **app/layout.tsx**
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics as VercelAnalytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Added `<VercelAnalytics />` component to the body section of the root layout
   - The component was aliased as `VercelAnalytics` to avoid naming conflict with the existing custom Analytics component
   - Positioned after the existing custom Analytics component and before BackendStatusBanner

2. **package.json**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies

3. **package-lock.json**
   - Updated with the new dependency and its transitive dependencies (414 packages total)

## Implementation Details:

- Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified the project uses Next.js App Router (confirmed by presence of `app/layout.tsx`)
- Identified npm as the package manager (confirmed by presence of `package-lock.json`)
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Followed the App Router setup instructions by adding the Analytics component to the root layout
- Preserved all existing code structure and functionality
- The existing custom Analytics component continues to work alongside Vercel Analytics

## Testing Performed:

✅ Build verification: `npm run build` - completed successfully
✅ Linting: `npm run lint` - no errors
✅ Tests: `npm run test` - all 35 tests passed (7 test suites)
✅ No TypeScript errors

## Next Steps for Deployment:

To enable analytics in production:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
2. Deploy the updated code using `vercel deploy`
3. Analytics data will start being collected automatically on all pages

The implementation is ready for deployment!
